  "limitations": [
    "This is fixture conformance on one Mac, not autonomous task reliability or arbitrary application support. Three trials per scenario do not establish production failure rates.",
    "CG-to-AX association uses unique PID, exact bounds and compatible available title metadata; public AX provides no OS-attested window-ID mapping, atomic validation/dispatch or reliable generation for same-role reuse with an unchanged or unavailable identifier.",
    "Advisory flock excludes cooperating new helpers for the same OS user; it does not exclude the human user, legacy helpers or other automation. Foreground endpoint samples cannot exclude transient or external changes.",
    "Only one-step AXSetValue, AXSelectedText replacement and AXPress are supported. Only exact-value waits and value/enabled guards or expectations execute. Images, OCR, keys, scrolling, coordinates, foreground delivery and multistep sequences remain later work.",
    "Private selection edits may be delivered while their public effect remains unverified; presses without an explicit observable expectation also remain unverified.",
    "Latency distributions mix different scenario workflows and exclude initial CG/AX readiness; they are not a matched performance comparison. Response-byte statistics count native structured JSON, excluding MCP framing and duplicate text content. No model tokens or monetary cost were measured.",
    "This branch is local and opt-in; no remote CI run, default npm entry migration, universal distribution or release is claimed. PER-3/PER-4 PR #9 is separately published with passing CI."
